# Docker build context for the Dockerfile (sub-phase 1.8). Keep the context to
# what the build reads: sources, the lockfile, Prisma, the shared UI package,
# the build scripts, and the LICENSE and NOTICE files every image carries.
# Adapted from inflect-compliance `.dockerignore` (PROVENANCE.md).

# Version control and CI
.git
.gitignore
.github
.husky

# Dependencies and build output: installed and rebuilt in the image
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
out
dist

# Tests and test tooling: the image never runs them
tests/
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
coverage/
jest.config.*
jest.setup.*
playwright.config.*
__mocks__/
eslint-rules/
eslint.config.*

# Documentation and deployment files: not read by the build
docs/
README.md
deploy/
docker-compose*.yml

# Environment files are secrets; never bake one into an image. The committed
# template is harmless, but nothing in the build reads it either.
.env*

# Editor and agent state (.claude/worktrees holds whole checkouts)
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/

# Logs and scratch
*.log
tmp/
